            <ArticleTitle>Dyspnea and Chest Pain in a Young Woman Caused by a Giant Pericardial Lymphohemangioma: Diagnosis and Treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1260.e23-1260.e25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0828-282X(15)01644-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cjca.2015.12.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 21-year-old woman who presented with chest pain and dyspnea on exertion and who was found to have a large pericardial mass. Multimodality imaging was instrumental in narrowing the differential diagnosis and planning surgical treatment, which included coronary artery bypass and right-sided heart reconstruction. The final pathologic diagnosis was lymphohemangioma; to our knowledge, this was the largest cardiac/pericardial vascular tumor ever to be reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
